    State the real closure rule on newly opened cases
    
    Independent review found the new case object still advertised the removed
    two-probe rule in durable state, contradicting the reconcile branch. New cases
    now carry the evidence-and-Judiciary-verification rule, and the smoke test
    asserts it. Correct the test comment so it matches the assertion that signal
    absence leaves the case open.

diff --git a/government/institutional-cases.py b/government/institutional-cases.py
index 84eac6eb..00881df2 100644
--- a/government/institutional-cases.py
+++ b/government/institutional-cases.py
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ def reconcile():
                     "legislature": "consider_evidence_and_legislation_if_needed",
                     "executive": "investigate_and_repair_within_existing_authority",
                     "owner": owner(signal),
-                    "closure_rule": "two independent healthy observations, not agent/process success",
+                    "closure_rule": "requires independent Judiciary verification of an evidence-backed investigation",
                 }
             case["last_seen"] = now
             case["observations"] = case.get("observations", 0) + 1
